@page "/privacy"
@using ChessLab.Web.Client.Services
@inject CurrentGameContext GameContext

<PageTitle>Privacy policy</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-espresso-soft">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>

<div class="mt-6 flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
    <p>
        Hand and Brain is a hobby project run by Michal Witko. This page explains what it knows about you
        and what it does with that.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">What we collect</h2>
    <p>
        You sign in with Google. From your Google account we receive your name, email address, profile picture
        and Google account identifier. We do not receive your password and we do not ask for any other
        Google data.
    </p>
    <p>
        We also store the games you finish: the room code, the game mode, the players, the result and when it
        ended.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">What we use it for</h2>
    <p>
        Your name and picture are shown to the other players in your room. Your identifier recognises you when
        you come back. Finished games make up your game history. Nothing is used for advertising or sold.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        We set one cookie to keep you signed in and another that protects the sign-in flow. We use no analytics
        or tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>
        The data lives in a PostgreSQL database and is served through our hosting provider. We do not share it
        with anyone else, except where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
        Write to <a class="text-amber-700 underline hover:text-amber-600" href="mailto:m.witko2000@gmail.com">m.witko2000@gmail.com</a>
        and your account and game history will be deleted. You can also remove the app's access in your
        <a class="text-amber-700 underline hover:text-amber-600" href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google account settings</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-700">Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>
</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => GameContext.Set(null);
}
